"epic net effect" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;epic-net-effect&gt;
		<header>The &lt;epic-net-effect&gt; element: the Net effect label over a short list of what a choice comes to.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>A "Net effect" list: what a choice, a reply or a change comes to, in a few bullets. It draws only the label, <text code>Net effect:</> or <text code>Net effect (A, recommended):</>; the list under it is the doc's own.</>

	<!--
		no <ui-list class="spell-meta">:  its <ui-item>s take Spell UI's "item" style sheet name before the
		              epics pack's elements can, and live examples may draw unstyled (issue I9 of epic-components)
	-->
	<text class="meta" paragraph>
		For anyone reading or writing an epic page's markup, or changing this element.

		Its vocabulary (every name it uses): <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-net-effect-epicneteffect-en-ts" link="/epic/src/components/epic-net-effect/EpicNetEffect.en.ts"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-net-effect/EpicNetEffect.en.ts" code>EpicNetEffect.en.ts</></>.

		Its component: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-net-effect-epicneteffect-tsx" link="/epic/src/components/epic-net-effect/EpicNetEffect.tsx"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-net-effect/EpicNetEffect.tsx" code>EpicNetEffect.tsx</></>, with its style sheet (<text code>.css</>) and tests beside it.
	</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<text paragraph>Three real ones: a question's recommended option (epic <text code>epic-components</>, J45, shortened), one option's (<text code>option="B"</>), and a plain one with a sentence (epic <text code>wwod-spell-ui</>, J70).</>
		<html>
			<epic-net-effect option="A" recommended>
				<ul>
					<li>new phase P12 · More Components, before Switch Over (now P13); Doc Review becomes P14</>
					<li>7 new <code>&lt;epic-*&gt;</> elements, 4 existing ones used in more places, the converter mapping each</>
				</>
			</>
			<epic-net-effect option="B">
				<ul>
					<li>anything goes</>
					<li>a light colour makes the white title unreadable</>
				</>
			</>
			<epic-net-effect>
				<p>static output unchanged; ssr tests 11/11.</>
			</>
		</>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>Live: the real element, drawn by the epics pack this page loads.</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Markup">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<text paragraph>As the epic-page rules show it (<link title="epic/templates/epics/plan-doc.md" target="src-spell-epic-templates-epics-plan-doc-md" link="/epic/templates/epics/plan-doc.md"><text code>plan-doc.md</></>, "Rules"), then a question's form:</>
		<text paragraph>plain, and one option's:</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<epic-net-effect>
			  <ul>
			    <li><code>D7 (Q3)</code> becomes <code>Q3</code>, answered</li>
			    <li>rule semantics changed: an answered question is no longer struck</li>
			  </ul>
			</epic-net-effect>
			<epic-net-effect option="A" recommended><ul><li>...</li></ul></epic-net-effect>
			```
		</>
		<text paragraph>Over a thousand live ones, in 942 files under <link target="src-epics" link="/epics/"><text code>epics/</></>.</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Where it goes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="map"/>
		<text paragraph>
			<text bold>Its parents:</>
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-list bulleted>
				<ui-item>Anywhere prose goes: it's a <dfn class="spell-term" tabindex="0">prose element</><ui-popup heading="prose element" label="An <epic-*> element marked flow in its vocabulary:  it goes wherever prose goes, so no parent has to list it."></>: <ui-list bulleted><ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-item-html" link="/epic-item"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-item&gt;</></>: among an item's own text, before its cards</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-answer-html" link="/epic-answer"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-answer&gt;</></>, <ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-more-html" link="/epic-more"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-more&gt;</></>, <ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-reply-html" link="/epic-reply"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-reply&gt;</></>: the cards under an item</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-option-html" link="/epic-option"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-option&gt;</></>: an option card's pros and cons</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-field-html" link="/epic-field"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-field&gt;</></>: a phase's field, or a labelled block</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-updated-html" link="/epic-updated"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-updated&gt;</></>: a change to a phase's plan</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-section-html" link="/epic-section"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-section&gt;</></>: an Overview sub-section's prose, or a report's</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-version-html" link="/epic-version"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-version&gt;</></>: an earlier version, kept as it was</> <ui-item>another prose element (a note inside an aside), or plain HTML around it (a <ui-text code>&lt;li&gt;</>, a <ui-text code>&lt;div&gt;</>)</></></>
			</>
		</>
		<text paragraph>
			<text bold>Its children:</>
		</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>prose: a <text code>&lt;ul&gt;</>, or a sentence or two in a <text code>&lt;p&gt;</></>
		</>
		<text paragraph>Every question, issue, judgement call and decision ends with one (an epic-page rule, 2026-10-04). A question's gives the recommended option's; each option may carry its own, inside its <text code>&lt;epic-option&gt;</>.</>
	</>

